 "cards": [
  {
   "dot": "emerald",
   "title": "One assistant, many agents",
   "items": [
    "The person talks to Harbor only; it delegates to specialists for intent, model, build, dashboards and cases",
    "Step Functions holds the build journey with three human-approval states: the brief, the understanding, go live",
    "Everything else runs without a person; EventBridge triggers monthly runs when files arrive"
   ]
  },
  {
   "dot": "rose",
   "title": "What leaves the account, and what never does",
   "items": [
    "Prompts reach Bedrock over PrivateLink, in-region, after the guard chain masks names and trims fields",
    "Rows, files and the DuckDB warehouse never leave the company bucket; groups under five are never shown",
    "No internet route from private subnets; the egress gateway is the only exit and logs every call",
    "Strictest option: a private model endpoint in the same account"
   ]
  },
  {
   "dot": "cyan",
   "title": "Security by layer",
   "items": [
    "Edge: CloudFront, WAF, Cognito SSO with MFA, one role per route",
    "Data: a bucket and KMS key per company, Aurora encrypted, Object Lock audit trail",
    "Agents: number guard on every answer, run IDs on every load, playbooks versioned in the control plane",
    "Tenancy: one AWS account per customer for sovereignty, or one VPC per customer in a shared account for cost"
   ]
  },
  {
   "dot": "violet",
   "title": "How the data engineer stays in the loop",
   "items": [
    "Escalation rules route a thread to an engineer when a source type is new, a shared table would change, or a match fails beyond tolerance",
    "The workbench shows model, mappings, SQL, runs and lineage, one click from any thread",
    "Autonomy per thread: Assist, Auto, Silent; it steps up only after clean months",
    "Evaluation gates: a pack ships only when its answer-key tests pass"
   ]
  }
 ]
}